#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:48
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:516
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:729
msgid ""
"Axolotl is a training framework that aims to make the process convenient "
"yet flexible to users by simply passing a config yaml file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:50
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:518
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:731
msgid ""
"As there are a lot of available options in Axolotl, this guide aims to "
"provide an simplify the user experience to choosing the proper choice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:52
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:520
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:733
msgid ""
"Axolotl supports 3 kinds of training methods: pre-training, supervised "
"fine-tuning, and preference-based post-training (e.g. DPO, ORPO, PRMs). "
"Each method has their own dataset format which are described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:54
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:522
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:735
msgid ""
"This guide will mainly use JSONL as an introduction. Please refer to the "
"dataset loading docs to understand how to load datasets from other "
"sources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:56
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:524
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:737
msgid ""
"For pretraining_dataset: specifically, please refer to the Pre-training "
"section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:58
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:526
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:739
msgid ""
"When aiming to train on large corpora of text datasets, pre-training is "
"your go-to choice. Due to the size of these datasets, downloading the "
"entire-datasets before beginning training would be prohibitively time-"
"consuming. Axolotl supports streaming to only load batches into memory at"
" a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:60
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:528
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:741
msgid "A sample format for a pre-training dataset is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:62
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:530
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:743
msgid ""
"It is typically recommended to save your dataset as .jsonl due to its "
"flexibility and simplicity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:64
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:532
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:745
msgid "Axolotl supports loading from a Hugging Face hub repo or from local files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:66
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:534
#: ../../source/references_dataset-formats.md:747
msgid ""
"As an example, to train using a Hugging Face dataset hf_org/name, you can"
" pass the following config:"
msgstr ""

